ENCReload — licence scope
=========================

This repository holds two kinds of material under DIFFERENT terms. Read this scope
first: the MIT grant reproduced below applies ONLY to the material listed in (1).

1. EDITOR CODE AND SCRIPTS — MIT (the grant below applies in full)

     Assets/Scripts/**   the HAF authoring tools: the Model Factory, the Animation /
                         Vehicle / District / Prop / Projectile / Sound Labs, the
                         bakers, the registries, and the editor CLI.
     Tools/**            the model-prep and build scripts: the Blender/Python rigging
                         and export helpers, glbconv, and the check gates.

   This is the same grant the framework itself carries — see the Humankind Asset
   Framework repository, which is MIT throughout:
   https://github.com/sswelm/HumankindAssetFramework

2. EVERYTHING ELSE IN THIS REPOSITORY — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED

   All content is reserved. That includes, and is not limited to:

     Assets/Databases/**        ENC's Humankind game data — civilizations, units,
                                traits, the tech tree, and every other definition.
     Assets/Pack/ENCReload/**   the ENC asset pack: pack.json, skins/, sounds/.
     docs/**, README.md, AUTHORING.md, and this repository's other prose.
     Unity project configuration (ProjectSettings/, Packages/, Assets/csc.rsp).

   No licence is granted for this material. It may not be copied, redistributed,
   repackaged, modified or reused without express written permission. Being able to
   read it here is not permission to ship it.

3. MATERIAL THAT IS NOT OURS TO LICENCE

   Neither (1) nor (2) grants anything over material owned by others:

   - The Humankind modding SDK and any decompiled game internals remain the property
     of Amplitude Studios. They are excluded from this repository by .gitignore and
     must be obtained from your own installation.
   - Third-party 3D models, textures and audio each remain under THEIR OWN licence,
     which governs regardless of (2) — several require attribution. See
     Assets/Pack/ENCReload/CREDITS.md.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The MIT grant referred to in (1) above. It applies to the paths named there, and
to nothing else in this repository.
